<title>GERMANY: Bilfinger+Berger lowers 96 dividend steady. [CORRECTED 14:16 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bilfinger+Berger lowers 96 dividend steady. [CORRECTED 14:16 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects title from 'Bilfinger+Berger holds 96 dividend steady)  - Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  92.4    vs 105.5</p>
<p>    Group transfer to reserves	    48.5    vs 55.8</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			 73.7    vs 84.0</p>
<p>    Parent transfer to reserves	   30.4    vs 35.4</p>
<p>    Dividend				    1.20    vs 13.50 marks</p>
<p>(Corrects previous year's dividend from 12 marks to 13.50 marks)</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German building group is Bilfinger + Berger AG. The dividend return is unchanged from 1995 as the nominal value of shares has since been cut to five marks from 50 marks.</p>
</text>
